/**

@brief BL1 K mission-FW launch, on device
@defgroup tests_bl1_mis_k_device BL1 K mission-FW launch, on device
@ingroup all_tests
@details
On-device tests for the BL1 K launcher (app/bl1/mis_launch_k.c), run unchanged.

The handshake registers, the staging area and the reset vector are the real SMC addresses. A
cooperative host thread plays the host: it writes STAGED after the launcher starts, then sets
VALIDATED once the launcher has requested validation.

Two calls are faked, because they leave the device:
- gr_smc_jump_to() never returns, so the tests only check that it was called.
- tt_chiplet_remote_boot_launch_mis() would load and boot real Mimir chiplets.

The launcher writes the reset vector before it jumps, so each test restores the original value
afterwards.

@section tests_bl1_mis_k_device_plan Test plan

| Test | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| test_empty_bundle_returns_without_jump | An empty TOC makes the launcher return with no chiplet launch and no jump. |
| test_wrong_type_returns_without_jump | An SMC BL1 image at TOC index 0 makes the launcher return with no jump. |
| test_valid_mis_launches_chiplets_and_jumps | A valid MIS bundle sets the reset vector and jumps to MIS. No chiplet launch: the test overlay has no chiplet_boot node, so that branch is not covered. |

@{
@}

*/
